{
  "about": [
    "One entry per shetach. territory lists what it covers: a US state or Canadian province (US-TX, CA-ON), a Mexican or Australian state (MX-JAL, AU-NSW), or a whole country (ISO 3166-1 alpha-3: FRA, DEU; ISR is all of Israel, including Judea and Samaria (the West Bank) and the Golan Heights); the part of a US state east and/or west of a longitude ({ \"state\": \"US-PA\", \"westOf\": -78.13 }); counties by 5-digit FIPS ({ \"counties\": [...] }); towns ({ \"state\": \"US-MA\", \"towns\": [...] }); census tracts ({ \"state\": \"US-MA\", \"tracts\": [...] }); regions of a country by their GADM name ({ \"country\": \"GRC\", \"level\": 2, \"regions\": [\"Central Macedonia\"] }; level 1 unless given); or a boundary shape from data/shapes/ inside a state ({ \"state\": \"AU-QLD\", \"shape\": \"brisbane-sua\" }).",
    "Where claims overlap, the more specific one wins: tracts, then towns and shapes, then counties and regions, then longitude lines, then whole states and countries. Anything no shetach claims is left blank.",
    "short: the label used where the name doesn't fit; by default the state and province abbreviations joined (KS-MO). capital: the chabad.org center id of the shetach's headquarters (the number in its chabad.org link), or lat and lon; \"world\": true marks 770. headTitle: what the card calls the head (\"Head shliach\" unless given, e.g. \"Leadership\"). lastName is optional; it defaults to the last word of headShliach. notShown: areas left off the map entirely."
  ],
  "notShown": [
    "CA-YT",
    "CA-NT",
    "CA-NU"
  ],
